# Dotfiles Context

Describes the chezmoi-managed dotfiles repository location so agents can
reference files and run commands without needing to be cd'd into the repo.

## Dotfiles Source Directory

```
{{ .chezmoi.sourceDir }}
```

When referencing files or running commands that need the dotfiles root, use the
path above.

## Chezmoi Rules

- NEVER use `chezmoi apply --force`. It blindly overwrites local changes.
- Before applying, always run `chezmoi diff` to preview what will change.
- If `chezmoi apply` fails with TTY issues ("could not open a new TTY"),
  investigate the conflict instead of forcing. The failure means a managed
  file has local modifications that would be lost.
- Prefer editing the source template in the dotfiles repo, then running plain
  `chezmoi apply` (without flags).
